# The beat, the eighth base element, one discrete tick of time. The knit and the wake each act once a beat. Time is the count of beats, and its one-way order, set by the lean and the wake, is the arrow.
form beat
  case tick

# The beat, proof-checked by `seed test`: one discrete tick of time, and time is the count of beats, whose one-way
# order is the arrow. A later beat is above an earlier: the count runs forward and cannot be reversed.
hold <a later beat is above an earlier beat>
  call is-above
    code 2
    code 1
